<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Goodman confident on purchase approval.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Goodman confident on purchase approval.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Food group Goodman Fielder Ltd said on Friday it believed it would win New Zealand Commerce Commission approval to buy the New Zealand operations of baking and milling group Defiance Mills Ltd.</p>
<p>Goodman chairman David Clarke said a number of matters needed to be finalised, in particular Commerce Commission approval, before the NZ$48 million acquisition was finalised by the end of April.</p>
<p>&quot;Our advice is that that will be forthcoming,&quot; he told a media briefing.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
